From b2a29db63b7a512273ddf5d7ef04d88fef59777a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 18:30:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 46/46] Daikin: track lifetime energy usage in-process, port of
 daikin-usage.sh

Replaces the external hourly cron script (daikin-gateway:/var/lib/domoticz/
scripts/daikin-usage.sh) with native tracking inside the plugin. Every poll
cycle, GetDayPower() checks whether the wall-clock hour has advanced since
the last credited bucket; on the first cycle after an hour rolls over it
fetches /aircon/get_day_power_ex and reads that hour's now-settled bucket
from curr_day_cool/curr_day_heat (24 "/"-joined 0.1kWh buckets), mirroring
the script's own awk field selection (1-indexed by hour-of-day, falling
back to field 24 at hour 0).

Three new kWh meter devices (node ids 43/44/45) carry the exact same Name
strings the old script's dummy-hardware devices used -- "Daikin usage",
"Daikin heat usage", "Daikin cool usage" -- since Grafana's InfluxDB tags
are keyed off that Name (confirmed: panel "Airco" queries tag name
"Daikin-usage", the slugified form of "Daikin usage"). idx/HardwareID are
not preserved; only the Name string continuity was required.

Because Domoticz restarts nightly, the running totals can't just live in a
member variable seeded at construction -- RestoreUsageTotals() reads each
device's own last stored value back via CSQLHelper::GetLastValue() on first
use, including the DeviceStatus row's LastUpdate hour, so a restart that
lands inside the same hour a bucket was already credited in doesn't
double-count it.

The old cron script's "Domoticz looks confused, fall back to a /tmp cache
file" branch has no equivalent here: the plugin holds the authoritative
running total in memory for its whole lifetime and only ever reads the DB
once, at startup.

Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>

Assisted-by: claude:claude-sonnet-5 [Bash] [Edit]
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [WIP]
Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
